<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Niskala Wastu Kancana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th–15th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Prabu Raja Wastu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Niskala Wastu Kancana was a Sundanese king of Galuh in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> who ruled from Kawali in the 14th and 15th centuries. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/astana-gede">Astana Gede</a> inscriptions at Kawali record him fortifying the town and urging his successors to rule justly. His grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-baduga-maharaja">Sri Baduga Maharaja</a> inherited both <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunda-strait">Sunda</a> and Galuh in 1482, uniting them under the capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakuan-pajajaran">Pakuan Pajajaran</a>.</p></div>
